msgstr ""

#: ../../benchmarks.rst:847
msgid ""
"Anubis is a capable, widely deployed product, and these rows are not a "
"claim that it is slow. It runs on a garbage-collected runtime, signs "
"sessions with Ed25519 by default so that verification needs no shared "
"secret, offers several challenge methods and a rich policy language, and "
"keeps challenge state in a store; those are design choices with benefits "
"this harness does not measure. The rows show what a request cost each "
"product on one host under one load shape, in October 2026. Sibuna is new, "
"and these are its first measurements beside an established product."
msgstr ""

#: ../../benchmarks.rst:849
msgid "Console Overhead"
msgstr ""

#: ../../benchmarks.rst:852
msgid ""
"SID 0007 sets the console's isolation contract. Enabling the console may "
"cost at most 1% of data-plane throughput and at most 10% of p99 latency, "
"measured over a matrix of configurations (compiled out, compiled in but "
"disabled, idle, and eight active dashboards) and workloads, with repeated "
"interleaved runs and reported uncertainty. Inconclusive or noisy runs do "
"not establish compliance, and primitive baselines and smoke runs cannot "
"substitute for the gate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../benchmarks.rst:854
msgid ""
"SID 0010 records one measurement: with the console compiled in, disabled, "
"storage only, or enabled and idle, the 16 product workloads stay within "
"about 1% of the daemon built without it, which is within noise. The "
"record names no result file for it. The configuration with eight active "
"dashboards under load has not been measured, so the formal gate of SID "
"0007 remains open."
msgstr ""

#: ../../benchmarks.rst:856
msgid ""
"The eight-dashboard run checks function, not overhead. ``sibuna-browser "
"dashboards`` started a release daemon on one SQLite node with its "
"console, four workers and a policy that allows ``/static/*``, ``/about``, "
"``/missing/*`` and ``/broken/*`` and challenges everything else; an "
"origin fixture answers ``/missing/*`` with 404 and ``/broken/*`` with "
"500. A generator sent 200 requests per second for 30 seconds, rotating "
"ten paths (one an SQL injection), three User-Agents and 500 forwarded "
"addresses. Each dashboard ran in its own Chromium with its own session: "
"dashboards 1 to 3 as administrator sessions, dashboards 4 to 8 as wall "
"displays opened with codes the first one minted, because the console "
"allows five sign-ins per minute per address and per account."
msgstr ""

